{# ─── SERVICES IN TRINITY BEACH ─── #}
<section class="copy-block">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Painting Services — Trinity Beach</span>
    <h2>What we paint in Trinity Beach</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:14px">Most jobs we get called for in Trinity Beach fall into a handful of buckets. We do the full residential side, plus light commercial work (cafe fit-outs, units, strata).</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Exterior repaints</h3>
    <p>Full strip, prep, prime, and topcoat with a coastal-grade exterior system. We do the render touch-ups, replace soft timber, treat any existing mould, and seal everything tight before topcoat goes on. Most exterior repaints in Trinity Beach take 4–7 days on-site depending on house size.</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Eaves, soffits, fascia</h3>
    <p>These take the worst of the salt and UV. We strip flaking coatings back, treat any rot, prime with a stain-blocker, and finish with two coats of UV-stable exterior. Done right, it lasts another 7 years easy.</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Interior repaints</h3>
    <p>Walls, ceilings, trim, doors. We mask off, fill, sand, and prime properly so the topcoat sits flat. No paint splatter on your floors when we leave.</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Pool houses + outdoor entertaining</h3>
    <p>Coastal pool surrounds, outdoor kitchens, pergola timber — these all need a marine-grade finish. We use Sikkens on timber and Dulux Weathershield on rendered surfaces.</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Fences + outdoor timber</h3>
    <p>Hardwood fences, screen panels, decks. Strip back to bare timber, oil or stain, finish with a UV-stable topcoat.</p>

    <h3 class="subhead">Roof painting + roof restoration</h3>
    <p>Tile, Colorbond, and corrugated. Pressure clean, re-screw if needed, treat rust spots, then spray with a heat-reflective system that drops indoor temperatures and your power bill.</p>
  </div>
</section>

