    <div class="faq-list">
      <details open>
        <summary>How often should I repaint my Trinity Beach exterior? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>Most Trinity Beach exteriors need a proper repaint every 5 to 7 years. Salt mist and wet-season humidity break down cheaper coatings faster than inland. If you're still on builder's-grade paint from when the place was built, you'll be due now.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What's the best exterior paint for a coastal Cairns home? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>We use Dulux Weathershield and Solver Aquashield on render and masonry — both are formulated for tropical coastal conditions. For timber (eaves, fascia, decks) we go with Sikkens. The paint matters but the prep matters more — even the best system fails over a bad surface.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you do interior repaints in Trinity Beach too? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>Yep. Full interiors, single rooms, or just a refresh on the high-traffic areas. We mask off, fill, sand, prime, and finish — your floors and furniture stay clean. Most three-bed interiors take 5–8 days depending on prep.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are you fully insured and licensed? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>Yes — fully insured, QBCC-licensed, and trade-qualified. Happy to share the QBCC number on quote.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you charge for quotes? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>No. The site visit and quote are both free, and the quoted price is fixed — what we write down is what you pay.</div>
      </details>
